.TH ENGINE_SHUTDOWN 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
engine_shutdown \- Pop every remaining scene (their on_exit runs, top first), stop services in reverse order (text, audio, textures, gamepad, renderer, window) and quit SDL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqengine.h\(dq
.BI "void engine_shutdown(Engine *e);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pop every remaining scene (their on_exit runs, top first), stop services in reverse order (text, audio, textures, gamepad, renderer, window) and quit SDL. Safe to call after engine_run returns; call it exactly once. Sounds loaded with audio_load() that were not freed in an on_exit are leaked, harmlessly, at this point.
.SH MODULE
core (src/engine/core/engine.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine_init (3),
.BR engine_run (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
